ght:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Don&#x27;t wait for a reason to smile </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/Xaeg2o5hmQqV74T222hdkfiaGE4=/0x0:1920x1080/1920x1080/2026/06/15/1781538578246.jpeg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of a hand with a wooden classroom pointer pointing at a smiley face on a chalkboard\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>Your smile could be</strong> a self-fulfilling prophecy.</p><ul><li><strong>Why it matters: </strong>Simply smiling when you're stressed or blue can lift your spirits, research shows — even when you don't totally feel it.</li></ul><p><strong>🔎 Zoom in: </strong>Several studies have found evidence that the physical act of smiling can boost feelings of happiness.</p><ul><li><strong>People who smile</strong> while performing stressful tasks tend to have lower heart rates than those with neutral expressions, Judy Ho, a Los Angeles clinical and forensic neuropsychologist, <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48143694.323279/aHR0cHM6Ly9hcG5ld3MuY29tL2FydGljbGUvc21pbGluZy1oZWFsdGgtYmVuZWZpdHMtM2RiOTU5MGNhZGI0ZmQwNjJjMDk3N2E3ZTBmYWJiYjA_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB262755d6\" target=\"_blank\">told AP</a>.</li><li><strong>Smiling while running</strong> can help you relax and run more efficiently, <em>Outside Magazine </em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48143694.323279/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cub3V0c2lkZW9ubGluZS5jb20vaGVhbHRoL3RyYWluaW5nLXBlcmZvcm1hbmNlL3NtaWxpbmctbWFrZXMteW91LW1vcmUtZWZmaWNpZW50LXJ1bm5lci8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBe41d5847\" target=\"_blank\"><em>reports</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>The intrigue: </strong>The findings support the idea that physical actions and sensations can help shape emotions, rather than simply reflect them, <em>Stanford researchers <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48143694.323279/aHR0cHM6Ly9uZXdzLnN0YW5mb3JkLmVkdS9zdG9yaWVzLzIwMjIvMTAvcG9zaW5nLXNtaWxlcy1jYW4tYnJpZ2h0ZW4tbW9vZD91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBaa6e0364\" target=\"_blank\">write</a></em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48143694.323279/aHR0cHM6Ly9uZXdzLnN0YW5mb3JkLmVkdS9zdG9yaWVzLzIwMjIvMTAvcG9zaW5nLXNtaWxlcy1jYW4tYnJpZ2h0ZW4tbW9vZD91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCaa6e0364\" target=\"_blank\"></a>.</p><ul><li><strong>A smile, </strong>even a forced one, can make us feel happier. A furrowed brow can spark feelings of anger.</li></ul><p>🎒 <strong>Case in point: </strong>At the Orange County Academy of Sciences and Arts in Southern California, the power of a smile is taken very seriously. An entire section on the charter school's website is dedicated to its philosophy that a smile can make a difference.</p><ul><li><strong>\"Smiling creates</strong> a supportive classroom culture that makes students relaxed, active, and motivated,\" according to the website. \"It increases emotional well-being, lowers stress, and gives students confidence.\"</li></ul><p><strong>Smiling isn't a magic fix.</strong> One <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48143694.323279/aHR0cHM6Ly9wdWJtZWQubmNiaS5ubG0ubmloLmdvdi8zMDk3MzIzNi8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBf2c3f2c1\" target=\"_blank\">analysis of 138 studies</a> found that the emotional benefits of facial expressions are modest and vary depending on the circumstances.</p><ul><li><strong>But it's a free,</strong> instant tool to keep in your back pocket next time you're feeling down.</li></ul><p><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48143694.323279/aHR0cHM6Ly9hcG5ld3MuY29tL2FydGljbGUvc21pbGluZy1oZWFsdGgtYmVuZWZpdHMtM2RiOTU5MGNhZGI0ZmQwNjJjMDk3N2E3ZTBmYWJiYjA_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aC262755d6\" target=\"_blank\">Go deeper</a>.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48143694.323279/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtZTMyOGQyODItYTY2YS00NTk0LWI4YTktMTc2YTE2NTI0MjM4Lmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB9c2664d7\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48143694.323279/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvb